# Simply supported beam: deflection under a uniform load

The mid-span deflection is $d_{max} = 5 q l^4 / (384 E I)$ and the rotation at a support is
$\varphi_{max} = q l^3 / (24 E I)$.

## Inputs
l: 6 m | beam length
q: 30 kN/m | uniform load
I: 160000 cm^4 | second moment of area
E: 30 GPa | modulus of elasticity

## Results
EI: E * I -> kN*m^2 | flexural rigidity
d_max: 5 * q * l^4 / (384 * EI) -> mm | maximum deflection, at mid-span
phi_max: q * l^3 / (24 * EI) | maximum rotation at a support, in radians
d(x): q / EI * (x^4 / 24 - l * x^3 / 12 + l^3 / 24 * x) | deflection along the beam

plot -d(x * 1 m) / (1 mm) for x in 0..l / (1 m)
